WEBVTT

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.050
<i>Why are they attacking the 
medicine and not us?</i>

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.050
<i>Do they actually understand 
the value of that?</i>

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.980
<i>Do they know who we are?</i>

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.500
<i>Could they be</i>

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.080
<i>the same group that attacked 
Bugs 2 twenty years ago?</i>

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.550
Eva! Run!

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.450
No! Eva, run! Run!

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.450
Let go! Let go of me!

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.210
<i>More importantly, how long 
have they been here?</i>

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.960
<i>How did they get in?</i>

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.640
<i>What orders are they following?</i>

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.950
<b><i>To the Planet of Calamity</i></b>

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.550
<i>You're going to head back to Earth?</i>

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.190
Yes. Our samples will be the

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.520
five or six terraformars 
that infiltrated our ship.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.550
In accordance with the mission manual, 
we are already heading back to Earth.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.770
Open up!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.270
<i>That will not happen, Captain Komachi.</i>

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.170
<i>Six samples aren't nearly enough.</i>

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.740
<i>The future of humanity as 
well as twenty years' worth</i>

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.200
<i>of funds are riding on this mission.</i>

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.400
<i>Failure is not an option.</i>

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.670
<i>Continue with Plan Delta.</i>

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:55.540
Plan Delta was for if we 
could not return in our main vessel.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.970
<i>Believe, Captain Shokichi.</i>

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.270
<i>As long as you have your 
higher-ranking officers,</i>

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.810
<i>they will protect the lower-ranking officers 
and complete this mission without fail.</i>

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.820
I've seen a horde of roaches

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.010
shoot down a spaceship that was taking off.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.690
But where are we right now?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.030
We're above Mars's thermosphere!

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.450
They wouldn't be able to get in here 
on their own, even if they tried!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.600
Are you implying they just wandered in
 because they knew we're here?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.540
Or were they hiding here in the first place?!

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.180
Either way, there's no point talking

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.790
to you guys since all 
you care about is money.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.040
It's obvious that someone planned this!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.390
We're falling.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.940
M.A.R.S Ranking?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.700
Yes. It's how they rank their ability to suppress

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.900
the cockroaches in the environment on Mars.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.710
Starting with Captain Komachi, 
the six executive officers...

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.950
It wouldn't be much of a stretch 
if I called them weapons.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.210
Weapons...?

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:20.070
But weapons are dangerous.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.280
That seems heavy, Michelle-san.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.490
Let me give you a hand.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.100
They are in position to command Annex 1,

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:37.310
and come from military backgrounds.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.820
They are not antipersonnel 
or anti-cockroaches.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:45.740
Japan,

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.490
Germany,

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:48.950
China,

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:50.990
America,

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.740
Russia,

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.500
and Roman Commonwealth.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:06:00.450
They are anti-terraformar professionals 
chosen from all of those countries.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.480
Well done coming here first.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.630
You were very brave.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.190
Captain.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.390
I'll take care of things here.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.760
You head to the escape vessels.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.120
Eh?

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.150
Apparently they've infiltrated 
other areas, as well.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.060
Joe and Liu, head to the 
crew's residential quarters.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.750
Asimov, the storehouse.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.780
Adolf, protect the escape vessels 
that are in the hangar.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.840
<i>This is Komachi Shokichi, 
the captain of Annex 1.</i>

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.790
We will commence Plan Delta.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.550
<i>Currently, the main engine has been damaged</i>

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.160
<i>and we are gradually falling toward Mars.</i>

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.250
<i>Because a safe landing in this 
vessel has become difficult,</i>

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:58.990
<i>all personnel need to head to 
the escape vessel hangar area.</i>

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:00.490
Y-You say that, but... How?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.450
You're all right now.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.450
Leave this to me.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:18.730
All of you hurry and head 
to the escape vessels!

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.870
Captain!

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.720
Are you going at it?

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.160
Oh, there're two right there.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.140
Wow, damn.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.780
Don't you think there are 
too many of your friends?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.280
Don't you guys have anything better to do?

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.200
Everyone, please calm down.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.170
The escape vessels are right here.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.290
Wait, Alex!

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.790
Marcos, Akari-kun!

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.050
Thank goodness you're safe!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:14.050
The Captain said there might 
be roaches here, too...

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.030
Everyone get back.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.570
Get back.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.180
Vermin.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:03.790
So strong...

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.000
It appears that there are 
six roaches that got in.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:35.670
<i>Coincidentally, the same number 
as the executive officers... huh?</i>

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.230
Eva.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.610
Clean it up. It's dangerous if it's wet.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.760
All troops, at attention!

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:06.270
I'm sure there's a lot 
that you want to say...

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.370
But this is how it is.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:12.280
Captain Komachi will explain the plan.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:14.900
Everyone, listen carefully.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.210
In accordance with emergency Plan Delta,

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:23.200
we will now commence landing on Mars

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.220
using the six high-speed escape vessels.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:29.380
The Japanese and American No.1 division, 
will be led by me.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.020
The Japanese and American No. 2 division, 
will be led by Michelle.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:39.060
No. 3 division, Russia and 
Scandinavia, will be led by Asimov.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:43.570
No. 4 division, China and 
Asia, will be led by Liu.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.830
No. 5 division, Germany and South 
America, will be led by Adolf.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:53.660
No. 6 division, Europe and 
Africa, will be led by Joseph.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.540
To avoid the possibility of all 
of us being attacked at once,

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.680
we will go in six separate directions.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.630
However, once we land we 
will communicate via radio,

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:05.060
and rendezvous where 
the main vessel crashes.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.240
Got it?

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:07.430
Yes, sir!

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:09.290
Let's go!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.070
Sheila-chan... Everyone...

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.030
It'll be okay, Eva.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.550
Everyone will be in different divisions,

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.070
but all of the executive 
officers are really strong.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.590
Everyone... stay alive.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.010
Let's see each other again on the surface.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.110
There are no signs of roaches nearby.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.400
Let's head out.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.130
I've

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:50.600
seen photos an unmanned vessel took 
of Mars in the 20th century, but...

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.990
It's completely different.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:58.980
After five hundred years, 
it's come this far...

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.480
If there was nothing else, 
it'd be a beautiful planet.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.240
What are you admiring 
the view for, you idiots.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:16.700
We're not on a picnic.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.960
Though we were lucky to 
land near some water.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.340
Despite the frozen soil starting to melt,

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:25.800
there's still very little compared to Earth.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.900
Shall we find out if it's safe or not?

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:30.160
Yeah.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.640
Just in case, we have enough 
drinking water for forty days,

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.390
but the more usable water 
we have the better.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.850
There are ladies in our division, as well.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.390
Ladies? Who would that be?

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:41.860
Who knows?

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.150
I'm going to contact the other divisions.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.750
Don't let down your guard.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:51.970
Those annoying bastards might 
be as close as one hill over.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.520
Y-Yes, Ma'am.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.230
You can take off your masks.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.810
I can... actually breathe.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:17.390
I thought the oxygen level here was 
about the same as the top of the Andes.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.920
That's amazing.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.280
I guess this is another result of the surgery.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.430
<i>Damn it... There isn't that much medicine.</i>

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:31.450
<i>Considering we were originally 
planning to stay on the Annex.</i>

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.980
<i>The supply here is just reserves.</i>

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:40.710
I wonder if everyone else is okay.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.370
I wonder if they were able to land safely.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:53.440
At least we weren't immediately surrounded.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.010
Yes...

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.440
This is Michelle K. Davis from 
the No. 2 division speaking.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:12.970
<i>All other divisions, come in and report if 
you were able to make a safe landing.</i>

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.700
Wow, Michelle-san was fast. 
Did they land nearby?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.830
We're...

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.470
A net?

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.920
What?!

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.670
No!

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:57.370
Good grief...

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:02.040
So this is why all six vessels 
flew in different directions.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.990
We might have picked the short straw.

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.400
I heard that twenty years ago,

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:11.990
there were beings of high 
intelligence present, but...

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.510
To think that they were this intelligent...

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.730
We ended up pretty far.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.020
We might be far from any other division...

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:28.300
Of course. What might our 
coordinates be, Elena-chan?

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:30.300
I'm not sure.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:33.990
Our satellite is down. 
Where were you hoping for?

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.850
However, I know where we are.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:40.740
We did it, Captain.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.040
Indeed. It's all according to plan.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:50.850
We've landed!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.870
So they do exist...

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.680
Yeah, though it's just sand.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:07.910
It's surprising that the cockroaches 
haven't gathered here.

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:10.160
I'm definitely not complaining 
if they're not around, though.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:14.050
Well, let's get started on our mission.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.720
They weren't on the radar before...

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.960
It's like they came out of nowhere.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.240
Just one? How amusing.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.000
Elena! We're going with Sign B.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:48.830
Right!

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.660
Bring out the net.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.950
It's just one!

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.360
Save the medicine!

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:01.040
Just like in our training, 
we're going to take that idiot back alive.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.870
I'll shoot! Everyone follow my lead.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.540
Sis!

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.190
If you or the Captain did it, you'd kill it.

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.690
And don't call me "Sis" during our mission.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.480
<i>It's heading straight for Sis.</i>

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.400
<i>It's just like the captain said.</i>

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:22.720
<i>But...</i>

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.010
Concentrate, Ivan.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.180
We're going to save the medicine, 
but don't let go of it, either.

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:31.290
If the roach is heading right 
toward Elena, we should be fine.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.350
If you give Elena a cannon, 
she's the best in the northern sea.

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:40.390
Especially with the propelled 
anti-terraformar bug net.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.280
Target...

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:49.040
locked!

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.990
There's nothing on the radar... All right.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:35.990
We're going to move.

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.350
Everyone, I'll say this again.

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:47.120
Now that Plan Delta is in place,

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:50.020
there should be a rescue vessel 
heading for us from Earth.

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:53.810
In forty days, that rescue 
vessel will land on Mars

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.190
and we will return to the Earth.

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:59.020
While we wait for that, 
we have two missions.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:03.400
First, rendezvous where the Annex crashed.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.710
Bring the virus research 
equipment back online,

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:09.270
and bring back a sample of the Mars Virus.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.490
And in the meantime, 
don't get killed by any roaches.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:17.240
First, we will regroup with 
Michelle and the No. 2 division.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:21.500
As soon as we regroup with the 
other higher-ranking officers

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.300
that we can trust,

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.800
we will recover Annex 1!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:25.950
Yes, sir!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:30.310
<i>Christian Era April 12th, 2620.</i>

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:35.020
<i>The Mars research team lands on Mars.</i>

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:38.880
<i>The mission to obtain the Alien Engine Virus,</i>

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:42.100
<i>and to fight terraformars,</i>

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.480
<i>has begun.</i>

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.910
<i>There are forty days until 
the rescue vessel from Earth</i>

00:21:57.340 --> 00:21:58.880
<i>lands on Mars.</i>

00:23:35.080 --> 00:25:40.230
<b><i>All-Out War</i></b>
